{"book":19,"chapter":5,"rubric":"PROCESSES AND RESOURCES / CHAPTER 5","slides":[{"title":"Three kinds of hitting a wall","sub":"Chapter 5 · Processes and resources","short":"Symptoms","main":"A limit, a priority and memory shortage look different.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Limit","Fork","Priority","Memory"],"captions":["A limit: \"Too many open files\" (EMFILE)","A fork fails: \"Resource temporarily unavailable\"","Priority: the process lives but gets little CPU","Memory: the process vanishes, the kernel log shows the killer"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"EMFILE: too many open files","tone":"red","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"EMFILE: too many open files","tone":"red","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"EAGAIN: cannot create a process","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"EMFILE: too many open files","tone":"red","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"EAGAIN: cannot create a process","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n2","x":180.0,"y":90.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"alive but starved of CPU","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"EMFILE: too many open files","tone":"red","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"EAGAIN: cannot create a process","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n2","x":180.0,"y":90.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"alive but starved of CPU","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n3","x":180.0,"y":122.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"killed for lack of memory","tone":"violet","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[7.4,16.4,25.3]}]},{"title":"ulimit: soft and hard","sub":"Chapter 5 · Processes and resources","short":"ulimit","main":"Flags -S and -H; without flags both values change.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Soft","Hard","Both!","Soft only"],"captions":["ulimit -n: the soft value, the one enforced","ulimit -Hn: the hard ceiling","ulimit -n 4096 without flags changes both values","ulimit -Sn 4096 changes only the soft one; the ceiling stays"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["$ ulimit -n","1024","$ ulimit -Hn","524288","$ ulimit -n 4096     # soft AND hard","$ ulimit -Sn 4096    # soft only"],"hl":[0,1],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["$ ulimit -n","1024","$ ulimit -Hn","524288","$ ulimit -n 4096     # soft AND hard","$ ulimit -Sn 4096    # soft only"],"hl":[2,3],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["$ ulimit -n","1024","$ ulimit -Hn","524288","$ ulimit -n 4096     # soft AND hard","$ ulimit -Sn 4096    # soft only"],"hl":[4],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["$ ulimit -n","1024","$ ulimit -Hn","524288","$ ulimit -n 4096     # soft AND hard","$ ulimit -Sn 4096    # soft only"],"hl":[5],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}]],"cues":[8.8,14.4,24.2]}]},{"title":"/proc/PID/limits and prlimit","sub":"Chapter 5 · Processes and resources","short":"prlimit","main":"A running process's limits can be seen and changed without a restart.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Table","Units","prlimit","Change"],"captions":["/proc/PID/limits: name, soft, hard, units","unlimited means no restriction; nice has no units","prlimit -p PID --nofile reads the same numbers","--nofile=8192: sets the soft value; only a privileged user raises the hard one"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["$ cat /proc/1234/limits","Max open files   1024    524288   files","Max processes    63704   63704    processes","$ prlimit -p 1234 --nofile","NOFILE  open files  1024  524288  files","$ prlimit -p 1234 --nofile=8192:"],"hl":[0,1,2],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["$ cat /proc/1234/limits","Max open files   1024    524288   files","Max processes    63704   63704    processes","$ prlimit -p 1234 --nofile","NOFILE  open files  1024  524288  files","$ prlimit -p 1234 --nofile=8192:"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["$ cat /proc/1234/limits","Max open files   1024    524288   files","Max processes    63704   63704    processes","$ prlimit -p 1234 --nofile","NOFILE  open files  1024  524288  files","$ prlimit -p 1234 --nofile=8192:"],"hl":[3,4],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["$ cat /proc/1234/limits","Max open files   1024    524288   files","Max processes    63704   63704    processes","$ prlimit -p 1234 --nofile","NOFILE  open files  1024  524288  files","$ prlimit -p 1234 --nofile=8192:"],"hl":[5],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}]],"cues":[7.1,15.6,23.6]}]},{"title":"Where limits come from","sub":"Chapter 5 · Processes and resources","short":"Sources","main":"An SSH login and a service get limits by different paths.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Kernel","Login","Service","Children"],"captions":["The first process gets the kernel values, children inherit a copy","A login (SSH, console): PAM reads limits.conf and limits.d","A service: the unit sets the limits, there is no PAM session","Children keep the parent's limits, even across execve"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"kernel: values of PID 1","tone":"muted","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"kernel: values of PID 1","tone":"muted","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"login: pam_limits + limits.conf","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"kernel: values of PID 1","tone":"muted","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"login: pam_limits + limits.conf","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n2","x":180.0,"y":90.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"service: LimitNOFILE= in the unit","tone":"violet","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"kernel: values of PID 1","tone":"muted","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"login: pam_limits + limits.conf","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n2","x":180.0,"y":90.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"service: LimitNOFILE= in the unit","tone":"violet","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n3","x":180.0,"y":122.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"child = copy of the parent","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[10.2,19.3,28.7]}]},{"title":"The limits.conf format","sub":"Chapter 5 · Processes and resources","short":"limits.conf","main":"Domain, type, item, value; a specific entry beats a general one.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Fields","Asterisk","Group and user","limits.d"],"captions":["Four fields: domain, type (soft, hard, -), item, value","* means everyone; the most general entry","A user beats an @group, a group beats *","limits.d is read after the main file, by name, *.conf only"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["# /etc/security/limits.d/90-app.conf","# domain type item   value","*      soft  nofile 4096","@ops   -     nofile 65536","alice  hard  nproc  200"],"hl":[1],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["# /etc/security/limits.d/90-app.conf","# domain type item   value","*      soft  nofile 4096","@ops   -     nofile 65536","alice  hard  nproc  200"],"hl":[2],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["# /etc/security/limits.d/90-app.conf","# domain type item   value","*      soft  nofile 4096","@ops   -     nofile 65536","alice  hard  nproc  200"],"hl":[3,4],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["# /etc/security/limits.d/90-app.conf","# domain type item   value","*      soft  nofile 4096","@ops   -     nofile 65536","alice  hard  nproc  200"],"hl":[0],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}]],"cues":[9.8,17.1,24.2]}]},{"title":"Service limits in the unit","sub":"Chapter 5 · Processes and resources","short":"Unit","main":"LimitNOFILE= in the unit, DefaultLimit* in system.conf, the nr_open ceiling.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["One number","A pair","Default","Ceiling"],"captions":["LimitNOFILE=65536 sets both the soft and the hard value","LimitNPROC=4096:8192 is soft:hard; infinity removes the limit","DefaultLimitNOFILE= in system.conf applies to all units","You cannot go above fs.nr_open; fs.file-max is the system-wide cap"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["# app.service.d/limits.conf","[Service]","LimitNOFILE=65536","LimitNPROC=4096:8192","# /etc/systemd/system.conf","DefaultLimitNOFILE=1024:524288","$ cat /proc/sys/fs/nr_open","1048576"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["# app.service.d/limits.conf","[Service]","LimitNOFILE=65536","LimitNPROC=4096:8192","# /etc/systemd/system.conf","DefaultLimitNOFILE=1024:524288","$ cat /proc/sys/fs/nr_open","1048576"],"hl":[3],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["# app.service.d/limits.conf","[Service]","LimitNOFILE=65536","LimitNPROC=4096:8192","# /etc/systemd/system.conf","DefaultLimitNOFILE=1024:524288","$ cat /proc/sys/fs/nr_open","1048